James sought a reliable way to obtain evenly spaced draws from a multivariate distribution in R, recalling a technique similar to a "Latin Hypercube Sampling" (LHS). I explained LHS and how it could be implemented using the `lhs` package, highlighting the generation of samples and the subsequent transformation into desired distributions using `mvrnorm` and `qnorm`. James pointed out the issue with using `mvrnorm` and the potential loss of covariance structure through independent transformations. I clarified that using LHS requires direct sampling from the multivariate distribution to maintain covariance. I proposed generating LHS samples and then applying `mvrnorm` to incorporate the multivariate structure correctly. I also recommended exploring copulas for more complex dependence structures if desired.
